        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Does Dick's Sporting Goods sell treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes, sporting goods chains like Dick's typically sell home treadmills, both in stores and online. Selection varies by store and over the year, and the website often lists more than any one store has on display. Call ahead if you want to try a specific machine.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Are Dick's treadmills good?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              They are typically mainstream home treadmills, so quality depends on the specific model rather than the store. Judge each one on continuous horsepower, running surface, maximum user weight and warranty, and compare it line by line with the nearest mainstream model from the same manufacturer.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you try treadmills at Dick's?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Often, yes — many stores have floor models, which is one of the main advantages of buying there. Wear your own shoes, walk and run at your usual speeds, use the incline and fold the machine. Floor selection varies, so check whether the model you want is on display before visiting.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does Dick's deliver and assemble treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Delivery and assembly options vary by item and location and can change, so ask at the store or check the product page. Find out exactly where delivery stops, whether assembly is included or charged separately, and whether packaging is removed.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the return policy on treadmills at Dick's?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Large fitness equipment can carry its own return conditions, and policies change. Before paying, ask how long the return window is for that treadmill, whether it must be unassembled or boxed, whether there are fees, and how a return would physically happen.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Will Dick's price match a treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Check the current price-match policy, which sets which competitors and items qualify. Price matching typically requires the identical item, which can be difficult when model numbers differ between retailers. Compare the delivered and assembled price rather than the headline figure.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
